## Foreword

There is no one reason I am making this site, some reasons years in the making.
So please forgive me some meandering while I try to sort out the biggest few.

During my years of projects I've been rescued countless times by hundreds of
people ranging from stack overflow commenters, bloggers, forum posters, discord
members, my dad, and in one case a professor in Italy that kindly responded to
my confused email. I'd like to follow in those footsteps for the generations
after me. Perhaps this site will help someone.

Many times I've talked to people about my work and then been unable to access my
files or unsure where I stashed them. It's common advice to build a portfolio
for such occasions, and moreso for use in professional or paid environs; where
I've been a time or two. Perhaps this site will be handy for showing my
projects.

Many sites are ever more locked behind account, payment, or invitation walls. Or
designed to occupy you for longer than reason and natural desire warrants. Or of
ambiguous lifespan. I find it troubling that my personal access to my personally
curated and constructed materials be contingent on unceasing adherence to a
large and fluctuating Terms of Service. If rulers were to confiscate your
notebooks for being deemed a rude and unhappy person we'd all rightly recoil in
horror. Perhaps this site will help easily retain and rehost my work should the
worst come to pass.

For these reasons, and for improving my skills, I make this personal site. I
hope that what I've made here is of some profit to you, that I do not waste your
time on what is neither helpful nor beautiful. But I am not the judge of that
and it's high time I get out of your way.
